<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<!-- Chapters are enclosed with <chapter> tags. Use xml:id to -->
<!-- uniquely identify the chapter.  The @xmlns:xi attribute  -->
<!-- is needed if you use xi:include in this file             -->
<chapter xml:id="ch_third" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">

<!-- Change title when you have one: -->
  <title>Energy</title>
  <!-- If the chapter has sections, there may be an introduction -->
  <!-- before those sections. Note the <p> tags around content.  -->
  <introduction>
    <p>Energy is the physical quantity which does things for us. All bodily functions, from 
    thinking to lifting weights, require energy. Energy is needed to do any kind of work. 
    It move cars along the road and boats on the water. It cooks food on the stove 
    and keeps ice frozen in the freezer. It helps our body to grow and minds to think. 
    Energy is a changing, doing, moving, and working things. 
    Energy is the ability to produce change or do work. Due to energy we have light, heat, 
    sound, motion, and growth. Technologies, survival of life, and even existance of universe depend 
    upon energy. To understand energy we need to understand the work first.
 </p>
  </introduction>

  <!-- Sections can be written directly here, but it might help  -->
  <!-- with organization to include them as separate files.      -->
  <!-- That way it is easy to include the section in a different -->
  <!-- chapter later if you change your mind about the order.    -->
  <xi:include href="./sec_third-intro.ptx" />
  <xi:include href="./sec_third-conserv.ptx" />
  <xi:include href="./sec_third-examples.ptx" />

  <!-- One or more of the sections of a chapter might be exercises-->
  <xi:include href="./ex_third.ptx"/>
</chapter>
